      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;The Kingdom of Bright Moon has banned magic fourteen years ago, despite Princess Glimmer and Prince Adora having shown signs of magical potential from an early age. Now they turn twenty and remain untrained, oblivious of their true power. The ban on magic was declared the day the Royal Mage was to be chosen between their historical tutor, Light Spinner, and the Kingâ€™s sister, Castaspella, who got elected. It was known that Light Spinner could not handle defeat or frustration, yet no one could have guessed sheâ€™d curse her and swear to take revenge on the regents. Queen Angella immediately banned magic, forwent her own magic to keep her daughters safe, and all sorcerers had to abandon Bright Moon or swear never to use their magic again, like King Micah did. Since then, Light Spinner, now Shadow Weaver, has cursed several people, motivated by mere â€œaggravationâ€, while Castaspella remained in the Whispering Woods, attentive to her every move, doing her best to counter the curses. Some could be lifted, yet she could only partially reverse the curse on those suffering her same fate. Neither Princess Glimmer nor Prince Adora should know the true story; Queen Angella has decided magic is now a threat, and so it must remain.&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
